Let me pull read-only data on your three resources and whatever else is wired to them (compute, networking, backups) in eu-central-1.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_qWlq5jHejxnvFQDq91QHLP", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Run read-only AWS checks on three named data stores in eu-central-1 for a disaster-recovery resilience assessment. Return RAW STRUCTURED FINDINGS ONLY (data rows), not a narrative report or investigation write-up -- this feeds a report I am writing myself.",
  "context": "This is a disaster-recovery / resilience posture check, NOT a root-cause investigation. The customer runs an application backend in eu-central-1 with: an Amazon RDS MySQL instance named dr-demo-mysql, an Amazon ElastiCache Valkey replication group named dr-demo-valkey, and a DynamoDB table named dr-demo-players. They have no RPO/RTO targets yet and want to know where they stand against: (1) single-service failure, (2) AZ failure, (3) Region failure, (4) bad data (accidental delete/bad write). Use only read-only describe/list AWS API calls -- make no changes.",
  "resources": ["dr-demo-mysql (RDS for MySQL)", "dr-demo-valkey (ElastiCache Valkey replication group)", "dr-demo-players (DynamoDB table)", "region: eu-central-1"],
  "timeframe": "current state (not time-bounded)",
  "criteria": "For each resource, make these calls and report the fields:\n\nRDS (dr-demo-mysql): rds describe_db_instances -> MultiAZ, BackupRetentionPeriod, DeletionProtection, StorageEncrypted, ReadReplicaDBInstanceIdentifiers, AvailabilityZone, Engine/EngineVersion. rds describe_db_snapshots -> manual and automated snapshots, which Region they are in. rds describe_db_instance_automated_backups -> any automated backups replicated to another Region. rds describe_source_regions (called from eu-central-1) -> which Regions eu-central-1 can pair with for cross-Region automated backups / read replicas.\n\nElastiCache (dr-demo-valkey): elasticache describe_replication_groups -> number of member clusters/replicas, AutomaticFailover, MultiAZ, SnapshotRetentionLimit, GlobalReplicationGroupInfo (is it part of a Global Datastore?), node type/family. elasticache describe_snapshots -> existing backups and which Region holds them.\n\nDynamoDB (dr-demo-players): dynamodb describe_table -> Replicas field (is it a global table?); if access denied, note that replica info could not be read and fall back to describe_continuous_backups/list_backups only. dynamodb describe_continuous_backups -> PointInTimeRecoveryStatus and RecoveryPeriodInDays. dynamodb list_backups -> any on-demand backups and their dates.\n\nAWS Backup (covers all three): backup describe_region_settings -> whether DynamoDB advanced features (ResourceTypeManagementPreference.DynamoDB) are turned on, since that gates whether AWS Backup can copy DynamoDB backups cross-Region. backup list_backup_plans and backup list_protected_resources -> are any of the three resources in a backup plan? backup list_recovery_points_by_resource for each of the three resource ARNs -> do recovery points actually exist (not just plan membership)? Note: AWS Backup does NOT support ElastiCache -- don't expect protected-resource entries for it.\n\nReturn the result as one row per resource using this exact scheme: layer | resource | type | Region | in-Region redundancy (AZs, nodes, replicas) | backups (kind, frequency, retention) | copies outside Region | point-in-time recovery status | replication status | what could not be read (denied/skipped calls). Do not write prose conclusions or recommendations -- just the data."
}", "deep_research": false}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check RDS MySQL, ElastiCache Valkey, and DynamoDB DR posture in eu-central-1."}, {"id": "tooluse_XoaQ20olE6V4ZMsOlxIMni", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Discover what else is part of this application workload in eu-central-1 beyond the three named data stores, and check the redundancy of shared dependencies. Return RAW STRUCTURED FINDINGS ONLY (data rows), not a narrative report -- this feeds a resilience report I am writing myself.",
  "context": "This is a disaster-recovery / resilience posture check, NOT a root-cause investigation. The named resources are: RDS MySQL instance dr-demo-mysql, ElastiCache Valkey replication group dr-demo-valkey, and DynamoDB table dr-demo-players, all in eu-central-1. I need to find what compute (EC2/ECS/EKS/Lambda), load balancers/entry points, and networking connect to these three resources, since a Region failover is only as good as its weakest layer. Use only read-only describe/list AWS API calls -- make no changes.",
  "resources": ["dr-demo-mysql", "dr-demo-valkey", "dr-demo-players", "region: eu-central-1"],
  "timeframe": "current state (not time-bounded)",
  "criteria": "1. Find the workload: cloudformation list_stacks and list_stack_resources in eu-central-1 looking for a stack containing any of the three resource names, or named/tagged like 'dr-demo'. Also try tag GetResources for tag keys like app/application/project/workload/Name with values containing 'dr-demo'. Report every stack/tagged resource found.\n2. If compute is found connected to these resources (EC2 instances, Auto Scaling groups, ECS services, EKS node groups, Lambda functions): check whether it spans multiple AZs (ec2 describe_instances, autoscaling describe_auto_scaling_groups, ecs describe_services as applicable) or is a single instance/task -- a single point of failure.\n3. Entry and routing: elbv2 describe_load_balancers (note Availability Zones attached) and describe_load_balancer_attributes if any load balancer is found in the same VPC/stack. route53 list_health_checks and any hosted zone records for failover routing.\n4. Network: find the VPC these three resources sit in (from their subnet-group/VPC config -- rds describe_db_instances DBSubnetGroup, elasticache describe_replication_groups, dynamodb has no VPC). Then ec2 describe_nat_gateways and describe_route_tables for that VPC (checking for a single zonal NAT gateway serving multiple AZs), and ec2 describe_vpc_endpoints (checking AZ coverage).\n5. Secrets and KMS: secretsmanager describe_secret for any secret tied to these resources (note ReplicationStatus/replica Regions). If RDS/ElastiCache/DynamoDB are encrypted with a customer-managed KMS key, note the key and that cross-Region copies would need an equivalent key in a recovery Region.\n6. Report every finding as one row using this exact scheme: layer | resource | type | Region | in-Region redundancy | backups | copies outside Region | point-in-time recovery | replication | what could not be read (denied/skipped calls). If nothing is found for a layer (e.g. no compute, no load balancer), say so explicitly as its own row rather than omitting it. Do not write prose conclusions or recommendations -- just the data."
}", "deep_research": false}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Discover connected compute, networking, and entry-point resources around these data stores."}], "created_at": null}

